---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const updated = "July 10, 2026";
---
<Base
  title="backlex — Refund Policy"
  description="How cancellations and refunds work for backlex paid plans."
>
  <section class="relative z-[1] max-w-[760px] mx-auto px-8 max-md:px-5 py-20">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 mb-12">
      <span class="inline-block self-start font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-muted-foreground border border-border rounded-full px-3 py-1.5 bg-muted">
        Legal
      </span>
      <h1 class="font-display font-light text-[clamp(32px,5vw,48px)] -tracking-[0.03em] leading-[1.05]">
        Refund Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="text-[13px] text-muted-foreground">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-8 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
      <p>
        This Refund Policy explains how cancellations and refunds work for paid
        plans of the backlex managed cloud ("the Service", "we"). It forms part
        of, and should be read together with, our
        <a href="/terms" class="text-foreground underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary transition-colors">Terms of Service</a>.
      </p>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-[19px] font-semibold text-foreground -tracking-[0.02em] mb-3">1. Free plan</h2>
        <p>
          The Free plan requires no payment card and is never charged. When its
          limits are reached, the project pauses until you upgrade or export your
          data. There is nothing to refund on the Free plan.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-[19px] font-semibold text-foreground -tracking-[0.02em] mb-3">2. Cancel any time</h2>
        <p>
          You can cancel a paid subscription at any time from your billing
          settings in the
          <a href="https://cloud.backlex.com" class="text-foreground underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary transition-colors">cloud dashboard</a>,
          or by emailing us. Cancelling stops the next renewal — your plan stays
          active for the remainder of the billing period you have already paid
          for, and then reverts to the Free plan. You will not be charged again.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-[19px] font-semibold text-foreground -tracking-[0.02em] mb-3">3. Refunds</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">
          Because you keep access to your paid plan until the end of the billing
          period you have already paid for, fees for the current period are
          generally non-refundable. If something went wrong — a billing error, a
          duplicate charge, or an accidental renewal — get in touch and we will
          review your request in good faith and refund where it is warranted.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 flex flex-col gap-2">
          <li>One-time charges and consumed usage-based add-ons (for example extra request packs, storage, or AI overage that has already been used) are non-refundable.</li>
          <li>Approved refunds are issued to the original payment method.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          This section describes our own refund practice. It does not affect the
          statutory rights described in section 4.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-[19px] font-semibold text-foreground -tracking-[0.02em] mb-3">4. Statutory right of withdrawal</h2>
        <p>
          If you are a consumer in Türkiye or the European Union, you have a
          statutory right to withdraw from a distance purchase within 14 days of
          the order. Because paid plans are supplied digitally and start as soon
          as you subscribe, you expressly request immediate supply at checkout
          and acknowledge that, to the extent permitted by applicable law, this
          right of withdrawal ends once supply has begun. Where the right still
          applies, contact us and we will arrange the refund through our Merchant
          of Record. Nothing in this policy limits any mandatory consumer right.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-[19px] font-semibold text-foreground -tracking-[0.02em] mb-3">5. Payments &amp; Merchant of Record</h2>
        <p>
          Payments for the managed cloud are processed by our Merchant of Record,
          <strong class="text-foreground font-medium">Polar</strong>
          (Polar Software Inc.), which acts as the seller of record and handles
          billing, tax, and the issuing of refunds on our behalf.
          Approved refunds are returned to the original payment method through
          Polar and typically appear within 5–10 business days, depending
          on your bank or card provider.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-[19px] font-semibold text-foreground -tracking-[0.02em] mb-3">6. How to cancel or request a refund</h2>
        <p>
          To cancel, open the billing settings in your cloud dashboard and use
          "Cancel plan", or email us. Your card details and invoices are managed
          in the Polar customer portal, which you can reach from the same page
          via "Manage subscription". To request a refund in the circumstances
          described above, email us at
          <a href="mailto:hi@backlex.com" class="text-foreground underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary transition-colors">hi@backlex.com</a>
          with your account email and the subscription concerned, and we will
          review and respond.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-[19px] font-semibold text-foreground -tracking-[0.02em] mb-3">7. Changes</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this Refund Policy from time to time. We will publish the
          updated policy on this page; the version in effect at the time of your
          purchase applies to that purchase.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-[19px] font-semibold text-foreground -tracking-[0.02em] mb-3">8. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For any questions about cancellations or refunds, contact us at
          <a href="mailto:hi@backlex.com" class="text-foreground underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary transition-colors">hi@backlex.com</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
